      }
    ],
    "observed_dialogue": [
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.15",
        "meeting_id": "ES2011b",
        "text": "And also we talked about um a location function where maybe you could press a button on the T_V_ and it would send sort of signal to the remote where it would beep or flash or vibrate or whatever to tell you where the remote is .",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.32",
        "meeting_id": "ES2011b",
        "text": "um we could use I_R_ but we'd probably wanna use radio instead .",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.33",
        "meeting_id": "ES2011b",
        "text": "That signal would go to a receiver which it would process it ,",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.34",
        "meeting_id": "ES2011b",
        "text": "and it would be output in the form of a buzzer or a light lighting up .",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.35",
        "meeting_id": "ES2011b",
        "text": "Um so my personal preferences for how to build the remote would probably be uh , battery for the energy source ,",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.39",
        "meeting_id": "ES2011b",
        "text": "I_R_ transmitter to communicate to the T_V_ ,",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.40",
        "meeting_id": "ES2011b",
        "text": "that's just sort of standard , um so most T_V_s have an I_R_ receiver .",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.41",
        "meeting_id": "ES2011b",
        "text": "Probably a radio receiver to send out location function and to receive it",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.42",
        "meeting_id": "ES2011b",
        "text": "and I'd probably say a buzzer for the location function on the remote itself .",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.14",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID",
        "text": "the user can input a channel or volume setting and it will be output to the T_V_ ."
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.16",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID",
        "text": "So the components we need are an energy source to power the remote ,"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.31",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID",
        "text": "And then for the location function , you would have a sender on the T_V_ which would output some sort of signal ,"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.36",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID",
        "text": "that way you wouldn't have to plug it in ,"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.38",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID",
        "text": "um we can purchase a pre-made chip which will handle all the processing stuff ,"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.43",
        "participant": "FEE042",
        "role": "ID",
        "text": "So that concludes my presentation ."
      }
    ],
    "peer_items": [
      {
        "item_key": "ES2011b#0",
        "type": "actions",
        "text": "The PM will check the updated project requirements (teletext removal, remote usage scope for television, corporate image) and update at the next meeting."
      },
      {
        "item_key": "ES2011b#1",
        "type": "problems",
        "text": "The hold-one-to-power idea would be hard to implement."
      },
      {
        "item_key": "ES2011b#2",
        "type": "problems",
        "text": "Users may be confused about powering the device if there is no separate power button."
      },
      {
        "item_key": "ES2011b#3",
        "type": "problems",
        "text": "There is uncertainty whether a screen is needed at all."
      },
      {
        "item_key": "ES2011b#4",
        "type": "decisions",
        "text": "PM(FEE041): teletext is apparently outdated , so <disfmarker> <vocalsound> due to internet popularity , so that's off the list . Um ,"
      },
      {
        "item_key": "ES2011b#5",
        "type": "decisions",
        "text": "UI(FEE043): So then our target age group would be the nineteen to thirty five range ,"
      },
      {
        "item_key": "ES2011b#6",
        "type": "decisions",
        "text": "PM(FEE041): Yeah , teenagers and young professionals ."
      },
      {
        "item_key": "ES2011b#7",
        "type": "decisions",
        "text": "PM(FEE041): so our remote should be used only for television , um ,"
      },
      {
        "item_key": "ES2011b#8",
        "type": "decisions",
        "text": "PM(FEE041): so if we had a like a kind of silver one like you saw , and yellow writing , something like that ."
      },
      {
        "item_key": "ES2011b#9",
        "type": "decisions",
        "text": "ID(FEE042): And also we talked about um a location function where maybe you could press a button on the T_V_ and it would send sort of signal to the remote where it would beep or flash or whatever to tell you where the remote is ."
      }
    ],
